r just a regular old mad scientist).<br /> <br /> And it's not a movie, but Richard Laymon's Resurrection Dreams was a more insidious, modern version, showing things from both sides (Melvin as the demiurge, and his creations which may or may not be Prometheans).<br /> <br /> Both of these are more in line with the bringing of the dead back to life, but not in the form of zombies. It's the themes and personalities that fit PtC more than the specifics.<br /> <br /> There is supposed to be a 'guy' version of May (this is how the review described it), I saw a page for it once on imdb but i never saw the movie myself (thinking May was perfectly fine) and I don't recall the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2013, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:28:40-08:00","id":47846,"title":"","content":"There is the movie Frankenweenie. It might be too lighthearted for some,but I liked it. If you don't mind a written source you might look at the short story Feathertop by Nathanial Hawthorne.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:51:13-08:00","id":48203,"title":"","content":"While it's full of narm for many, <b>Edward Scissorhands</b> is a good portrayal of a Created being not knowing how to live in the world or deal with people.<br /> <br /> Variations of <b>The Invisible Man</b> are good for showing what happens to someone on the Centimani path with the moral decay and celebrating being a monster. <b>The Fly</b>, especially the one with Jeff Goldblum is good for that, too.<br /> <br /> <b>The Island of Dr Moreau</b> for what happens when too many Prometheans get together with only a few to be the moral compass, and not all of them are quite right, either.<br /> <br /> For a wronged Promethean on a Torment-fuled warpath, Karloff's <b>The Man They Could Not Hang</b>. Kind of obscure, Karloff did a lot of these &quot;mad doctor&quot; movies and a lot of them could work for various situations, but this one is more specific as he's killed and brought back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-13-2014, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}